      "name": "Section Divider Rule",
      "role": "Horizontal hairline separator between major page sections",
      "description": "A 1px Parchment line stretching the full viewport width, interrupted in the center by a small italic section label (EditorialOld italic, 16px, Parchment) such as 'Work projects' or 'Lil projects'. At each end and at the center break, a small '+' crosshair sits on the line in Parchment — this is a signature motif and should appear on every major divider. Zero vertical padding above and below the line itself; the surrounding section gap is 51px."
